      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "KEVIN (4) opened this prep with a win and a close second on wet tracks then stepped up to 1100m last time on a good surface and was less effective. Conditions far more to his liking today. Very fit and should bounce back to his best form. BLUE DE BEERS (3) returns from a 24-week spell. Led all the way for a dominant win first-up last prep over 1100m at Bathurst. Lightly raced four-year-old who should kick this prep off in a positive manner. LIGHT INFANTRY (2) has raced at the provincials since an easy first-up win at Parkes. Scored over 1000m at his only attempt. Back in grade and should play a key role. Veteran CAPITAL MAC (1) has been freshened up since a couple of modest efforts to kick off this prep. Down in grade and comes in okay after the claim. Expecting a much better performance. THIRD BASE (6) goes fast and his best form comes at 1000m. Should be in this for a long way.",
